      "writtenOn": "2023-11-17T08:13:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sounds slightly over-specified to me. It\u0027s not wrong but in the context of this test it\u0027s not really essential to functionality that the current local prefixes are exactly the same as the received prefixes. Or in other words, you could change the impl of UNM in a way that is working but would fail this test.\nAnother way this could be a problem is if you call NotifyLinkProperties twice and then call this method twice : this would be correct usage, but the test would fail because the 1st check would find the result of the 2nd properties in mUNM.\n\nMaybe `any()` is sufficient here. You\u0027re just checking that the callback had a call to the correct LP. Or if you want to check the local prefixes, pass them as an argument.",
